{"v": 4, "date": "2026-11-19", "title": "Snow on the peaks Sunday 22 November, then a cold signal around Tuesday 15 December: what to expect in the coming weeks", "lead": ["For the next few days the high-resolution models lead: they see snowfall Sunday 22 November, about 30 cm at Monte Cusna (2121 m). It's a short episode, to be confirmed in the next updates.", "Beyond that episode no serious snow for now, but some scenarios bring cold air around Tuesday 15 December: that's the signal to watch in the next updates.", "We combined 297 scenarios from 8 different weather models, up to Friday 18 December.", "📉 Cooling down from Tuesday 24 November: snow possible, but only on the peaks"], "phases": [{"emoji": "🌧️", "label": "Next 5 days", "text": "From Thu 19 to Mon 23 the scenarios are split: Unsettled, snow only at high altitude 40 out of 100, Dry and mild 33 out of 100, Dry, temperatures around normal 24 out of 100. Snow: very unlikely (2 out of 100). Typical temperature at altitude around +6 °C, reliability medium. No model gives snow in at least 30 scenarios out of 100. The coarse-grid global models miss the snowfall on the peaks on Sunday 22 November that the high-resolution ones see: in these cases trust the local forecast.", "color": "#94a3b8"}, {"emoji": "🌧️", "label": "Days 6 to 10", "text": "From Tue 24 to Sat 28 the scenarios are split: Unsettled, snow only at high altitude 40 out of 100, Dry, temperatures around normal 31 out of 100, Snow up high, rain below 15 out of 100. Snow: unlikely (18 out of 100). Typical temperature at altitude around +4 °C, reliability medium. No model gives snow in at least 30 scenarios out of 100. The most promising day for snow is Thursday 26 November. Watch out for the cold: in 11 scenarios out of 100 it drops below −2 °C at 1500 m (the coldest down to -5 °C), especially around Thursday 26 November.", "color": "#94a3b8"}, {"emoji": "🌧️", "label": "Days 11 to 15", "text": "From Sun 29 to Thu 3 the scenarios are split: Unsettled, snow only at high altitude 36 out of 100, Dry and mild 33 out of 100, Dry, temperatures around normal 18 out of 100. Snow: unlikely (10 out of 100). Typical temperature at altitude around +5 °C, reliability medium. No model gives snow in at least 30 scenarios out of 100. The most promising day for snow is Sunday 29 November.", "color": "#94a3b8"}, {"emoji": "🌧️", "label": "Days 16 to 30", "text": "From Fri 4 to Fri 18 the scenarios are split: Unsettled, snow only at high altitude 31 out of 100, Dry and mild 30 out of 100, Dry, temperatures around normal 16 out of 100. Snow: unlikely (11 out of 100). Typical temperature at altitude around +4 °C, reliability low. No model gives snow in at least 30 scenarios out of 100. The most promising day for snow is Thursday 17 December. Watch out for the cold: in 20 scenarios out of 100 it drops below −2 °C at 1500 m (the coldest down to -6 °C), especially around Tuesday 15 December.", "color": "#94a3b8"}], "models": ["Between Tue 24 and Sat 28 the most convinced model is UK Met Office (29 snowy scenarios out of 100), the most sceptical GEM (9).", "The models broadly agree: a signal worth taking seriously."], "pros": ["Our estimate of the snow level on the ridge on days with precipitation: Thu 2800 m, Sun 2200 m.", "Levels still high: snow, if it comes, stays above 2200 m."], "big": ["The big picture points towards cold: the next model runs could add snow.", "NAO near zero in the second week: no clear push towards cold or towards high pressure (17 negative, 21 positive scenarios out of 100).", "Arctic Oscillation dropping sharply: polar cold air tends to slide towards mid-latitudes, Europe included.", "Sudden stratospheric warming: around Tuesday 10 November the stratospheric winds along 60°N reversed, from westerly to easterly (minimum -3 m/s); the vortex is now rebuilding (about 39 m/s around Friday 4 December). After such events the odds of cold air reaching Europe rise over the following 2–4 weeks: the window to watch runs from Tuesday 24 November to Tuesday 8 December. It raises the odds, it doesn't guarantee anything.", "How to read them together: the big picture says that cold is more likely than usual in the coming weeks; for now the models see it in 20 scenarios out of 100, while the rest stay unsettled and mild, with snow only at high altitude. If the cold is confirmed, that number will rise in the next updates: it's the signal to follow."], "weekend": ["Saturday: Good weather pretty much everywhere: pick the handiest spot.", "Sunday: The best spot is Lago Scaffaiolo. Top picks: Lago Scaffaiolo, Abetone, Cimone."], "ground": "For now the official stations measure no significant snow on the ground.", "chart": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 900 250\" class=\"syn-chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Temperature trend at 1,500 m\"><rect x=\"30\" y=\"101.9\" width=\"840\" height=\"60.1\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" opacity=\".7\"/><line x1=\"30\" x2=\"870\" y1=\"101.9\" y2=\"101.9\" stroke=\"#2563eb\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"115.9\" class=\"lbl snow\">❄ snow down to resorts below 0 °C</text><line x1=\"30\" x2=\"870\" y1=\"101.9\" y2=\"101.9\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/><polygon points=\"30.0,22.5 59.0,35.4 87.9,43.0 116.9,50.5 145.9,44.8 174.8,58.6 203.8,43.4 232.8,31.8 261.7,31.1 290.7,30.8 319.7,31.8 348.6,21.0 377.6,20.6 406.6,21.4 435.5,28.4 464.5,38.0 493.4,28.5 522.4,32.1 551.4,32.1 580.3,40.9 609.3,39.3 638.3,38.4 667.2,45.9 696.2,50.1 725.2,27.5 754.1,36.6 783.1,32.8 812.1,38.2 841.0,46.2 870.0,28.9 870.0,110.0 841.0,120.2 812.1,122.4 783.1,130.5 754.1,122.9 725.2,115.6 696.2,105.4 667.2,112.5 638.3,118.0 609.3,132.3 580.3,125.9 551.4,130.2 522.4,134.7 493.4,124.4 464.5,122.6 435.5,105.0 406.6,108.1 377.6,96.7 348.6,99.8 319.7,92.4 290.7,102.9 261.7,104.1 232.8,102.5 203.8,120.9 174.8,112.0 145.9,90.4 116.9,90.5 87.9,85.0 59.0,80.5 30.0,75.5\" fill=\"#0f2236\" opacity=\".09\"/><rect x=\"450.0\" y=\"6\" width=\"420.0\" height=\"156\" fill=\"#fff\" opacity=\".45\"/><text